From b0c05eb72e10140f87efd0e499ad840e6c3e6975 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GEEKiDoS <geek_ds@foxmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 18:02:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: qcom: add Lenovo Legion Tab Y700 Gen4 support

Enable the SM8750 Lenovo Y700 Gen4 with its NT36536 display and touch,
Peach wireless, camera sensors and ISP, AW88461 audio, haptics, and
sensor DSP. Describe board wiring and hardware constraints in devicetree
and retain the validated clock, SMMU, power-domain and USB sequencing.

Apply the board support and required dependencies to Linux 7.2. Adapt
DSI panel lifetime and bridge callbacks, PAS firmware handling, and I2S
clock setup to the 7.2 APIs. Include the panel DSC helpers, UFS ICE link,
Q6V5 handover IRQ lifetime fix and Clang BTI compatibility guard needed
by the tested configuration.

Preserve existing source attribution, including Pengyu Luo's original
board description and NT36536 panel work.

Validated with built-in drivers on the Y700 Gen4 using fastboot boot:
Wi-Fi transport, DRM CRC, camera frames, PCM playback, Zink/Turnip
rendering, SSC accel/gyro/light samples, RTC alarm and haptic replay.
The final V66f build also passes boot, config readback and display/sensor
checks. Image/DTB build, binding and full board DT validation pass.

USB-attached suspend still aborts with the existing EBUSY limitation;
post-abort display, audio, camera and sensor recovery was tested.
Bluetooth firmware setup and power-on work, but discovery did not pass.

Signed-off-by: GEEKiDoS <geek_ds@foxmail.com>
